summary_en:
Copies of records in the possession of Aboriginal Affairs and Northern Development Canada (AANDC), which touch on the events in May, 2011 which followed what we understand to have been an unusually heavy rainfall in the Smithers-Burns Lake area on approximately May 17, 2011. This request is intended to encompass the following:

   1) the analysis of Aboriginal Affairs of the entitlement of any geographical areas to government assistance including the Palling #1 Reserve of the Wet' suwet' en First Nation at Decker Lake B.C;
   2) the response to the offer of assistance or services by Aboriginal Affairs to any geographical areas including the Palling #1 Reserve of the Wet' suwet'en First Nation at   Decker Lake B.C.
   3) the provision of assistance or services by Aboriginal Affairs to any geographical areas including the Palling #1 Reserve of the Wet'suwet'en First Nation at Decker Lake B.C.;
   4) the construction of any buildings, roads, and/or any other construction related to flood mitigation in cooperation with Aboriginal Affairs to any geographical areas including the Palling #1 Reserve of the Wet'suwet'en First Nation at Decker Lake B.C; and
   5) any internal Aboriginal Affairs correspondence related to the flooding of the Wet' suwet'en First Nation at Decker Lake B.C.

summary_fr:
